told:
No more ... except the child!... no more at all.
I told your cousin, sir, that I was dead;
And now, she thinks I’ll get up from my grave,

tolled:
Yet, 'Croak, croak, croak,'
Still tolled from the oak;
From that fatal black bird,

The white clown caught it. From St. Rémy’s tower
The deep, slow bell tolled out the hour;
The black clown, with his dirty grin

tolls:
"I have no wish to barter souls;
My traffic does not ask such tolls.
I am no devil; is there one?

toleration:
Forgive me. To be blue and shrew at once,
Exceeds all toleration except yours;
But yours, I know, is infinite. Farewell.

tol:
An' I did n't know dey feelin's is de ve'y wo'ds dey said
W'en I tol' 'em I was so'y. Dey had done gin up dey all;
But dey only seemed mo' proudah dat dey men had hyeahed de call.
